# a remark of the review document under the title of a case
NOTE = {'columns of 0.50 m with the profile HEB 300 under a beam of 30.00 m of IPE 200: the far corner of what the menus allow': 'A test of the arithmetic, not an example of use: the beam carries 15 kN/m over 30 m, and the page shows a displacement of 7774.4 mm at midspan; the card “Large displacement” says that this lies outside the first-order theory of the page. The closed portal formulas and the analysis give F_Ax = 3 372.8 kN and a moment of 562.1 kNm at the base; the rigid limit in three steps of versions 9 to 12 gave 3 353.7 kN and 552.6 kNm here.',
        'cantilever of 6 m with 17 loads of 1000 kN downward at the tip and 0.1 kN along the beam': 'A test of the display, not an example of use: 17 000 kN at the tip of a 6 m cantilever is far beyond what the section bears. The tip moves 69.8 m, more than eleven times the span. The panel says in the card “Large displacement” that this lies outside the first-order theory of the page.',
        'support B set free and 20 kN hung on B: the column D–B hangs from the beam': 'The free end of the frame moves 0.53 m, and the column D–B turns by 72.9 mrad at its steepest place, more than 50 mrad: the panel says so in the card “Large displacement”.',
        '492.3 kN/m and 949.9 kN at 2.27 m: the shear reaches zero a third of a micrometre behind the load': 'A test of the marks, not an example of use: the loads are far beyond what the section bears. At the load the shear is 949.900167 kN before and 0.000167 kN behind it, and it reaches zero at 2.270000339 m. The beam also turns by 376.4 mrad at an end, more than 50 mrad: the card “Large displacement” says so.',
        'IPE 200, first bottom chord with 480 kN/m to the right and 576 kN to the left at 1.80 m: its axial force reaches zero at the load and steps to 576 kN behind it': 'A test of the numbers, not an example of use. The axial force of the chord falls from 864 kN at A to zero at the load, steps to 576 kN behind it and falls to zero at the end of the chord: a zero of the axial force falls on the load point. The load point moves 1.299248 mm along the chord (480 · 1.80² / (2 · 598 500) m) and 0.844511 mm downward, 1.5 mm in all.',
        'IPE 200, 294.4 kN at 2.27 m: the largest deflection, 300.0 mm, lies between two stations': 'A test of the display, not an example of use: the load is far beyond what the section bears. The beam deflects 300.012 mm at 2.793 m; the largest deflection at a station is 299.997 mm. The page reads the largest deflection on the line itself, also between two stations. The end A turns by 165.1 mrad, more than 50 mrad, and the card “Large displacement” stands.',
        '101 loads of 1000 kN at 0.01 m and 0.1 kN on A: the shear starts with the reaction less the load on A': 'A test of the display, not an example of use. The shear starts with 101 000.0 kN, the reaction is 101 000.1 kN: the 0.1 kN on A go straight into the support.',
        '20 kN along the beam at midspan under the 10 kN/m: the shear passes zero at that load without a step, and the peak is a smooth one': 'The load along the beam starts a piece of the lines and makes a step of 20 kN in the axial force, none in the shear: V is zero just before the load and just behind it. The moment line turns there smoothly, and the mark reads “V = 0: peak of M”, as it does without that load.',
        'a pin at A, rollers at B and C and 20 kN to the right on B: the axial force steps at a roller that carries a load along the beam': 'A roller has no reaction along the beam; the pin A holds the 20 kN. The rule “at a joint” of the axial-force tab gives the step with its sign: N right of B = N left of B − (F_x + P_x) = 20 − (0 + 20) = 0.',
        'IPE 200, span of 30.00 m with B fixed and an overhang of 1.40 m with 6400 kN at its end: the overhang is bent by more than its own length': 'A test of the display, not an example of use: the load is far beyond what the section bears. The end of the overhang moves P·L³/(3·EI) = 6400 · 1.40³ / (3 · 4 080.3) m = 1 434.7 mm and turns by P·L²/(2·EI) = 1 537.1 mrad. That is less than a twentieth of the span of 30 m and more than the overhang is long. The card “Large displacement” goes by the largest rotation of each member, names B–C and gives the 1 537.1 mrad. With 208 kN the end turns by 49.96 mrad, below the limit of 50 mrad, and the card is not shown; with 209 kN it turns by 50.20 mrad and the card stands.',
        'IPE 200, B fixed, 2 kN on the end of an arm of 0.50 m left of B and 95 loads of 1000 kN along the 30.00 m right of B: a deflection of 0.02 mm beside an axial force of 95 000 kN': 'A test of the display, not an example of use. The arm deflects 2 · 0.50³ / (3 · 4 080.3) m = 0.0204 mm at its end and turns by 2 · 0.50² / (2 · 4 080.3) = 0.0613 mrad there. The deflection would print 0.0 mm and carries no number; the rotation is written, −0.1 mrad. The line is drawn and is not called zero beside an axial force of 95 000 kN.',
        'IPE 200, cantilever of 30.00 m with 500 kN downward at 26 m, 1000 kN upward at 28 m and 500 kN downward at 30 m: the end turns by 490.2 mrad and moves less than a twentieth of the length': 'A test of the display, not an example of use: the loads are far beyond what the section bears. The moment is a triangle between 26 m and 30 m with −1000.0 kNm at 28 m: tension on top, a negative moment. Its area is −2000 kNm². The rotation changes by Δθ = −∫ M/EI dx, so the end turns by +2000 / 4 080.3 = +490.2 mrad, clockwise, and moves down by that rotation times 2 m, 980.3 mm: less than a twentieth of the 30 m. The card “Large displacement” goes by the largest rotation of a member and stands.',
        'IPE 200, hinge at B, roller at C and 30 loads of 1000 kN outward at each end of the arm B–C: the arm is a bar, stretched by a twentieth of its length': 'A test of the display, not an example of use. The arm carries N = 30 000 kN, no shear and no moment. It is stretched by N·L/EA = 30 000 · 3.00 / 598 500 m = 150.4 mm, 5.01 % of its length, and nothing turns. The card “Large displacement” says that the member is stretched by 5.0 % over its whole length, more than a twentieth, and names no rotation. With 29 loads at each end the arm is stretched by 4.85 % and the card is not shown.',
        'feet fixed, 40 kN/m inward on each column and 1.5 kN/m on the roof: the moment of the roof has a low point where its shear is zero': 'The roof has −17.1 kNm at both ends and −5.1 kNm at its middle, where its shear is zero: the moment line turns there, and the size of the moment is smallest. The card of the roof on the shear tab calls that place a low point. Where the size of the moment is largest at such a place the card says peak.',
        'height of 0.75 m and 100 kN/m to the right on the first diagonal: a load at 14 degrees to the bar also bends it': 'The diagonal is 3.09 m long and rises by 0.75 m. The part of the 100 kN/m across the bar is 100 · 0.75 / 3.09 = 24.3 kN/m: shears of +37.5 and −37.5 kN at its ends and a moment of +29.0 kNm at its middle. A load at so flat an angle is drawn beside the bar; the hint of its mark says that it also bends the member.',
        'IPE 200, hinge at B, roller at C, 60 loads of 1000 kN to the left at 1.00 m and 60 to the right at 1.10 m of the arm B–C: 10 cm of the arm are strained by 10.0 %': 'A test of the display, not an example of use. Between the two groups of loads the arm carries N = 60 000 kN: a strain of N/EA = 60 000 / 598 500 = 10.0 % over 10 cm. That lengthens the arm by 10.0 mm, 0.33 % of its 3 m. The card “Large displacement” goes by the largest strain of a member and names the stretch that has it. Up to version 15 it went by the lengthening of the whole member and was not shown here.',
        '20 kN upward and 20 kN downward at midspan under the 10 kN/m: the two loads cancel, no step of the shear and no kink of the moment': 'The two loads stand at one place and cancel. The shear is zero just before them and just behind them, and the moment line runs through with 45.0 kNm and no kink. The rules on the kink and on the step speak of the forces at one place together; the card of the member says that loads at one place count together.'}
def section(pg, name=''):
    """select the section of a case on the page; every other case gets the section the page starts with"""
    want = str(SEC.get(name, SEC0))
    if pg.input_value('#sec') != want:
        pg.select_option('#sec', want); pg.wait_for_timeout(450)
